{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.ConfinementSDP","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.ConfinementSDP","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.ConfinementLP","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.BorromeanUnique","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.GramIndefinite","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.sdp_lp_projection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.sdp_lp_projection","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L297-L303","doc":"**Scalar-LP projection — per-instance form.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.scalarLPProjection_of_strongDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.scalarLPProjection_of_strongDuality","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L282-L295","doc":"**`ScalarLPProjection` follows from strong duality.**\nThe identity `primalOpt = nTarget · y0Star` is exactly the\nstrong-duality statement, so any\n`[HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality n hSlater]` discharges the\n`agrees` field directly. The `bindingMultiplicity = 1`\nhypothesis is the qualitative scope marker (the LP-collapse\nregime); the algebraic content is the same. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ScalarLPProjection.agrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ScalarLPProjection.agrees","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L280-L280","doc":"Primal optimum agrees with the scalar LP optimum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ScalarLPProjection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ScalarLPProjection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L276-L276","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ScalarLPProjection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ScalarLPProjection","kind":"class","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L267-L280","doc":"**Scalar-LP projection — class.** When `μ(n) = 1`, the SDP\noptimum coincides with the scalar `markovTraceNF`-based LP of\n`QOU.Interactions.ConfinementLP`. The full proof requires an\nexplicit isomorphism between the diag-LP feasible polytope and\nthe rank-1 diagonal slice of the SDP feasible spectrahedron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.bindingMultiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.bindingMultiplicity","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L264-L265","doc":"Binding multiplicity accessor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasSDPBindingMultiplicity.mu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasSDPBindingMultiplicity.mu","kind":"def","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L262-L262","doc":"Active-dual-support cardinality `μ(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasSDPBindingMultiplicity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasSDPBindingMultiplicity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L260-L260","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasSDPBindingMultiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasSDPBindingMultiplicity","kind":"class","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L256-L262","doc":"Binding multiplicity data — class-supplied evaluation of `μ(n)`\n(cardinality of the active dual support at optimum). `μ = 1`\nrecovers the scalar LP; `μ ≥ 2` is the multi-operator regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.slaterStrict_is_freely_dischargeable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.slaterStrict_is_freely_dischargeable","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L221-L249","doc":"**The Slater hypothesis of `ConfinementSDP` is still freely\ndischargeable — by a different route since 2026-09-07.**\n\nIt used to be free because `slaterStrict` was a `Prop`-universe FIELD:\nthe instance supplied a proposition and `True` was legal. It is now the\nreal condition `∃ Φ, PosDef Φ ∧ Feasible Φ`, and the instance below\ndischarges it by choosing a trivial CONE instead — `PosDef` and\n`Feasible` both `fun _ => True`, witnessed at `Φ = 0`.\n\nKeeping this theorem is the point. The encoding narrowed the freedom\nwithout eliminating it, and a theorem that still proves the hypothesis\nfree is the honest record of exactly how much was bought: the shape of\nSlater's condition, not its content.\n\nNote the statement is `∃ inst, slaterStrict` and **not** `∃ _inst,\nTrue`: the latter says only that the class is inhabited, which is the\nweak discriminator this corpus already has an audit about\n(`2026-08-09-inhabitation-is-a-weak-discriminator`).  What is claimed\nhere is stronger and is the point — an instance whose Slater condition\n*holds*, by `trivial`.\n\nKept in the file deliberately, in the idiom of\n`TransferMatrixEigenphase`: a demonstration that a field asserts\nnothing is the honest record while the field cannot yet be encoded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.ConfinementSDP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.ConfinementSDP","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L146-L219","doc":"**Confinement SDP — primal–dual identity (conditional on a supplied\nduality identity; the Slater hypothesis is decorative).**\n\nStrong duality `⟨T, Φ*⟩ = n_target · y₀*` comes from the supplied\n`[hi : HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality n h]`, not from `h`.  The\nmanuscript argument is the conic-duality theorem (Boyd–Vandenberghe\n§5.2.3 + §5.3): under a strictly feasible `Φ ≻ 0` the dual is solvable\nand primal = dual.  That step is **not in Mathlib**, and this is\nmeasured rather than repeated:\n`docs/audits/2026-09-04-mathlib-infrastructure-inventory.md` §U7\nrecords `semidefinite program` **0**, `strict complementarity` **0**,\n`KKT` **0**, `duality gap` **0** and `LinearProgram` **0** at the\npinned revision, with no optimisation layer under `Analysis/Convex/`.\nTracked as bean `qou-apcl` (CONFIRMED).  So the step is supplied\nrather than derived.\n\n**`h : slaterStrict n` does no work, and can be discharged for free**\n(measured 2026-09-07, `lean`-direct exit 0; see\n`slaterStrict_is_freely_dischargeable` below).  `slaterStrict` is a\nfield typed with the *universe* `Prop`, so the instance chooses the\nproposition, and `slaterStrict := True` makes `h := trivial`.  The\nsignature therefore reads as Slater-conditional while constraining\nnothing.\n\n**That paragraph said this was \"not encodable here\". It was wrong, and\nit was mine (2026-09-07).** The reasoning — Slater is `∃ Φ ≻ 0\nfeasible`, and this class carries no constraint set and no PSD order,\n`R_q` being `LaurentPolynomial ℤ` — is all correct. The conclusion does\nnot follow: missing vocabulary is carried as fields, which is what\n`PosDef` and `Feasible` now are. `slaterStrict` is the condition itself.\n\nWhat survives of the caveat: an instance still chooses the cone, so the\nhypothesis is not thereby non-trivial in every model. See the note on\n`slaterStrict` for the exact scope of the improvement.\n\n**Two sentences here were false and were corrected on 2026-09-03**;\nthe lead sentence above was not among them and asserted, until\n2026-09-07, that strong duality \"is derived **from** the Slater-strict\nfeasibility hypothesis\".  It is not, and the paragraph below already\nsaid so — the correction reached the body and not the lead.\n\n**Two sentences here were false and are corrected (2026-09-03).** This\ndocstring said the step \"is discharged by `sorry` here\" and that \"the\ntheorem no longer merely projects that class field\". The body is\n`exact hi.strong_duality` and `#print axioms` reports no `sorryAx`: it\n*does* project, and there is no `sorry`.\n\nWhat it projects is legitimate, which is why only the prose changes.\n`[HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality n h]` is a conditional **input** a caller\nsupplies when they already have the duality identity (e.g. from a numerical\nSDP solver, via the `Fact`-backed default instance) — not a data field\npositing the conclusion. The in-body comment records that the earlier\nversion projected exactly such a data field, and that it was deleted. So the\nresult is conditional on Slater *and* on the supplied duality, and this\ndocstring now says so.\n\nCf. `markovTraceNF` in `ConfinementLP` for the scalar-LP\nprojection recovered when every Wedderburn block decouples. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.hasConfinementSDPStrongDuality_of_fact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.hasConfinementSDPStrongDuality_of_fact","kind":"instance","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L134-L144","doc":"**Default instance from a `Fact` witness on the strong-duality\nidentity**. When `Fact (primalOpt n = nTarget n * y0Star n)` is\nin scope (e.g. from a numerical SDP solver verifying strong\nduality at the specific `n`), the `HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality`\ninstance follows. Boyd-Vandenberghe Thm 5.5 lifts this to all\nSlater-strict `n` once Mathlib SDP duality lands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality.strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality.strong_duality","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Strong duality.\n(Needs abstract LP/SDP duality infrastructure that does not exist in Mathlib; kept as an honest assumption for models without certificates) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPStrongDuality","kind":"class","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L117-L132","doc":"**Confinement SDP — strong-duality typeclass.**\nHolds for `(n, h)` when the primal SDP\n`min ⟨T, Φ⟩ s.t. Φ ⪰ 0, ⟨π_λ, Φ⟩ ≥ 0, 2×2 pair-PSD, tr(Φ) = n_target`\nand its dual\n`max n_target · y₀ s.t. y₀ I + Σ y_λ π_λ − T ⪯ 0, y_λ ≥ 0`\nsatisfy strong duality `⟨T, Φ*⟩ = n_target · y₀*`. By\nSlater + Boyd–Vandenberghe Thm 5.5, this follows from the\nSlater-strict hypothesis once Mathlib SDP duality lands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.y0Star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.y0Star","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L98-L99","doc":"Optimal dual shadow price accessor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.slaterStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.slaterStrict","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L78-L96","doc":"**Slater's condition**: a strictly feasible point exists.\n\nWas `h.slaterStrict`, a field typed with the *universe* `Prop` — so the\ninstance supplied a proposition and `True` was a legal choice. It is now\nthe condition itself, `∃ Φ ≻ 0 feasible`, built from the cone and the\nconstraint set the class carries.\n\n**This narrows the freedom; it does not remove it, and saying otherwise\nwould be the over-claim.** An instance can still choose\n`PosDef := fun _ => True` and `Feasible := fun _ => True`, and\n`slaterStrict_is_freely_dischargeable` below still holds — with a\ndifferent proof. What changed is *where* the choice lives: the SHAPE of\nSlater's condition is now fixed (an existential over matrices conjoining\ntwo predicates) and only the cone is chosen, where before the whole\nproposition was. A model that supplies a real PSD cone gets a real\nhypothesis; before, no model could. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.nTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.nTarget","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L75-L76","doc":"Normalisation target accessor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.primalOpt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.primalOpt","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L72-L73","doc":"Primal-optimum accessor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.sdpCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.sdpCost","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L67-L70","doc":"Cost-operator accessor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.y0Star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.y0Star","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Optimal dual shadow price `y₀*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.Feasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.Feasible","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L63-L63","doc":"**The primal feasible set** — `⟨π_λ, Φ⟩ ≥ 0`, the 2×2 pair-PSD\nconditions and `tr(Φ) = n_target`, as one predicate. Carried for the\nsame reason: this class holds an optimum and no constraint set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.PosDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.PosDef","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L59-L59","doc":"**Strict positive-definiteness** on the block algebra.\n\nCarried as a field, not referenced: `R_q` is `LaurentPolynomial ℤ`,\nwhich has no order at all, so there is no `≻ 0` to appeal to. That\nabsence is what made the old `slaterStrict : Prop` look unavoidable,\nand carrying the cone is what makes it avoidable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.nTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.nTarget","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Normalisation target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.primalOpt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.primalOpt","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Optimal primal value `⟨T, Φ*⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.sdpCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.sdpCost","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Cost operator `T` of the confinement SDP. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.HasConfinementSDPData","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/ConfinementSDP.lean#L45-L65","doc":"**Per-`n` SDP data — class-supplied.** ","signatureChunk":0}]}